+- **B** — `--spec-type ngram-mod --spec-ngram-mod-n-max 128` (n-min left at default 48, n-match at default 24). Same family as A with a **larger draft window** (64 -> 128). Justification for choosing a variant of ngram-mod over a *different* ngram type (ngram-simple/map-k/map-k4v): (1) ngram-mod is the family the project has already characterized, so B is directly comparable to A and to the engine-review baseline; (2) it isolates one variable (draft window), the most likely knob to move acceptance on agent/mem traffic that re-emit long repeated context; (3) ngram-cache is a *draft-model* caching mechanism, not a self-spec n-gram type, and ngram-simple/map-k have never been probed on this model, so they are lower-signal for the 
